canonical.behaviour:
The /spar rework we agreed (agreement 1), in the worktree D:/workflow-axa-spar.
- Every message to you shows what a label means before the label: one rule in the shared writing guide, which grilling and spar point to.
- In /spar:
  - the two AIs agree or disagree per point in their own quoted words, with no exact-text rule and no separate synthesis round;
  - a spar ends when you can decide;
  - one start card, and questions that are ready asked together at the pause after the first answers;
  - an evidence step first, with your factual claims marked not yet checked;
  - a warning when only one model can debate;
  - plainer conclusions;
  - debaters told to read only, load no skills and ask no one.
- Tests that pinned removed sentences become behaviour checks; the safety checks stay.
- The docs describing /spar are updated, and the exact-wording tests are counted in a report only.
- Then the live test: the same replay cases as the before run, on the new version.
